language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session5_hardy_1729_square: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Find a combination of 4 different numbers between 1 and 100, such that the sum of the squares of the two first numbers is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two numbers, i.e. a^2 + b^2 = c^2 + d^2 for a, b, c and d between 1 and 100, all different.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session5_hardy_1729_square.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ the largest number allowed
letting maxv = 100
$ the four numbers a, b, c, d, each between 1 and maxv
$ a: the first of the two numbers whose squares are summed on the left
find a : int(1..maxv)
$ b: the second of the two numbers whose squares are summed on the left
find b : int(1..maxv)
$ c: the first of the two numbers whose squares are summed on the right
find c : int(1..maxv)
$ d: the second of the two numbers whose squares are summed on the right
find d : int(1..maxv)

such that
$ the four numbers are all different
allDiff([a, b, c, d]),
$ the sum of the squares of a and b equals the sum of the squares of c and d
a * a + b * b = c * c + d * d
